Dear S-News Readers,

I'd appreciate some help on how to interpret the residual deviance for a
GLM model using the binomial link function with a dichotomous (binary)
response variable. Briefly, I'm trying to compare two alternative
models. Both models include a factor variable, "country" as the first
variable, and the second variable is a quantitative variable whose
values range from 1 to 7. In the first model, I added the quantitative
variable as a simple linear term, and in the second model, I added the
variable as a piecewise linear term, which adds another degree of
freedom to the model specification.

