From GUIDO.MAGGIO at ESTERNI.GRUPPO.MPS.IT  Wed Jan  4 16:29:39 2006
From: GUIDO.MAGGIO at ESTERNI.GRUPPO.MPS.IT (MAGGIO GUIDO)
Date: Wed, 04 Jan 2006 17:29:39 +0100
Subject: Threshold EVT
Message-ID: <07B40C0AFE0DBE4FB7D979FF3135A92C012AC6B8@se000010010035.servinternet.local>

Dear Splus users

I am doing an Extreme Value Theory to analyze Loss data and I am estimating the Tail using a Generalized Pareto.

It's common problem here to determine the threshold that divides the tail from the body of the distribution. Graph techniques are the most used such as: Mean Excess Graph and Sum over Maximum for example.

However these techniques are subjective and do not identify an unique value of the threshold. I investigated and I got to know that there are some algorithms based on minimizing the MSE of the shape parameter of the GPD which can provide an unique solution for the identification of the threshold.

Danielson and DeVries (1997), Pictet at al. (1996) (a bootstrap method), Jansen and DeVries (1991) ( a Monte Carlo technique), and Berliant at al. (1996).

I wonder if any of you knows how to implement any of this algorithms with S+ of if you may have any suggestions

Thanks

Happy 2006 to all

Guido Maggio

